        "type": "reasoning_text",
        "text": "Now where's the persona section for 总管? It's a section, always injected when persona. I need to inject VERIFICATION_IRON_LAW after persona in lifecycle as its own section (key \"verification\"), and in the partner turn context text.\n\nDesign:\n1. New constants file? Task says put constants in existing family files: turn-gate.ts for VERIFICATION_IRON_LAW + RULING_DISCIPLINE + TAKEOVER_HINT; delegation.ts for REPORT_FOUR_LINES + WORK_SILENCE_DISCIPLINE + ATTENTION_ONE_QUESTION.\n\nInjection points:\n- VERIFICATION_IRON_LAW: after persona section in lifecycle (new section key \"verification_iron_law\") and in partner turn context (always, for partner turns). Should there be a switch? Task requires rollback switch only for #4 (AGENT_TAKEOVER_HINT). For others, no switch needed. But \"新能力给回滚开关\" in AGENTS.md... The task doesn't ask. Hmm. AGENTS hard constraint says new capabilities get rollback switch. These are prompt additions; adding 6 env switches would bloat. Task book explicitly only lists a switch for #4.5. I'll follow the task book (it overrides), but maybe add one switch for the whole batch? That adds complexity. The task book says for each new env; only #4.5. I'll not add extra switches, noting in change log that the prompt additions are reverted by removing constants... Hmm, \"至少留一行 env 退回上一形态\" is a hard rule. But adding 6 switches contradicts \"固定字节/简单\". Let me consider adding a single `AGENT_PROMPT_DISCIPLINE` switch? That's not in task book and would be invention.\n\nLet me check existing prompt constants: ATTENTION_REPLY_GUIDANCE has no switch; WORK_REVIEW_GUIDANCE no switch. So prompt-only additions in this codebase have no switches. Follow the established pattern (task book §〇.1: 照它们的写法). Only #4 gets a switch because it's mechanism/card text. Good.\n\n- RULING_DISCIPLINE: partner turn input (in partner-context text) + delegate tool description tail.\n- REPORT_FOUR_LINES: delegation.ts constant; consumed in delegate tool description (tell worker to report in four lines). Also maybe formatReport? \"改 delegation.ts 里给执事/总管看的汇报口径（formatReport 相关文案旁加常量 REPORT_FOUR_LINES）\" — just constant next to formatReport, consumed by tools.ts delegate description. Where else? Perhaps the partner status/report? Keep simple: define constant in delegation.ts near formatReport, and append a sentence in delegate description telling the planner to instruct the worker to report in four lines. Maybe also inject into partner turn input? Task says \"在 delegate 工具描述里补一句\". So consumption = tools.ts description.\n\n- WORK_SILENCE_DISCIPLINE: partner turn input.\n- ATTENTION_ONE_QUESTION: partner turn input (next to ATTENTION_REPLY_GUIDANCE), maybe also in delegate description? Task says only constant injection in partner turns. But #7.1 doesn't say explicitly where. \"放 delegation.ts，挨着 ATTENTION_REPLY_GUIDANCE\" — likely consumed in partner turn input too (where attention guidance is used) and/or tools description for the chief. The chief asks user questions too. Hmm, the section is \"注意力纪律\" (四#4). Likely the chief/partner when asking user. Let's inject in partner turn context and also in persona-side? The chief is not a partner turn (chief partnerId \"chief\" returns undefined for partner turn context, per lifecycle — actually partnerIdOfSession returns \"chief\" for chief session; partner-context builds context for any partnerId. But buildPartnerTurnContext in lifecycle runs for any partnerId including chief? Let's check: `if (partnerId)` → includes \"chief\". So chief also gets contract/status sections? buildPartnerStatusSection with chief's session ids... Hmm, presumably yes for goal/status. Wait the docstring says \"总管 / 主人会话（partnerIdOfSession=null）不注入\". Chief returns \"chief\" though... resolvePartnerScope treats chief specially for memory, but partnerIdOfSession returns \"chief\". So chief does get partner context. OK.)\n\nSo injecting ATTENTION_ONE_QUESTION and WORK_SILENCE_DISCIPLINE into partner turn context covers both chief and partners. For chief persona-side, #1 says VERIFICATION_IRON_LAW after persona.\n\nNow #4 failure-streak:\n- new file `failure-streak.ts` with pure state:\n```ts\nexport type FailureCategory = \"tool-error\" | \"timeout\" | \"rejected\" | \"needs_you\" | \"unresolved\";\nexport interface FailureStreakState { [key: string]: number } // serializable\nexport class FailureStreak { record(source, category): boolean; success(source, category?) ...}\n```\nDesign decisions: \"按 (来源, 类别) 记连续失败次数；成功一次即清零\". Which success? Probably `recordSuccess(source)` clears all categories for that source? Or same category? \"成功一次即清零\" — I'd implement `noteSuccess(source, category)` clearing that (source,category) and `noteSuccessForSource(source)`? Simpler API:\n\n```ts\nexport interface FailureStreakStore {\n  fail(source: string, category: FailureCategory): number;  // returns new count\n  reset(source: string, category?: FailureCategory): void;\n  count(source, category): number;\n  shouldSuggestTakeover(source, category): boolean; // count >= 3 and not yet signaled\n  snapshot(): Record<string, number>;\n  restore(data): void;\n}\n```\nNeed \"3 次触发一次\" — signal once at exactly 3? \"连续达 3 次 → 产出一次'建议人接管'信号\". Should repeat at 4,5? Probably trigger at >=3 but each fail beyond may also suggest; \"产出一次\" suggests once per streak. Use a `hinted` flag per key so it fires once until reset. But then unit test \"3 次触发\" straightforward.\n\nAlso \"不同类别互不干扰\". Key = `${source}\\u0000${category}`. Keys serializable. Sources include ticketId/domain? Use ticket domain or sender? In delegation.ts, source could be `kick.domain || ticketId`? \"来源\" = where failure came from, e.g. ticket id or domain. Task 4.4: 落点 delegation.ts 的 attention 事件发出处（540-548）与汇报行（349-350）各接一次. The attention event has ticketId and domain; failure category from attention kind? Mapping: `needs_you` for attention. In formatReport for needs_you. Where do we track failures? Need to record failures somewhere. 