igger until reset. Tests: 3rd triggers; 4th doesn't; success resets.\n\nFor attention event: question text appended with hint sentence:\n`question: takeover ? `${q}\\n（${TAKEOVER_HINT}）` : q` — but the shared schema DelegationEvent attention question is used by client. It's a prompt/文案 addition — acceptable (task says \"在 attention 卡片文案旁追加一句\").\n\nFor report line (349-350): formatReport's needs_you body. `formatReport` doesn't know takeover. Add optional param `takeover?: boolean` to formatReport, append to body. But report is truncated to 80 chars... hint sentence ~30 chars might get cut. Hmm, \"汇报行（349-350 附近）各接一次\". Maybe append hint to `result.attention.question` before report? Since formatReport takes result, and line 350 uses `result.attention?.question`. We can pass an option `{ takeoverHint?: string }` appended after the truncation? The task says append a sentence. Better append after the head/body and don't lose it: `truncate(...)` would cut. Could compute text then append hint, exceeding 80? 80 is 方案 fixed.\n\nAlternative: at 349-350, attach hint to the report's text in settle by constructing report then appending hint: `report.text = ...`? Hmm.\n\nCleaner: `formatReport(result, domain, options?: { takeover?: boolean })`, body for needs_you becomes `有一项需要你处理：${question}（这类问题已经连着 3 次没解决，建议你来接手，或者换个说法重新派一次。）`, then truncate to 80. The hint likely gets truncated out. But tests can assert the hint appears when we ask non-truncated? Hmm.\n\nMaybe increase? No.\n\nAlternative placement: mirror/REPORT line uses full `result.line`; the 80-char limit only for report.text (conversation one-liner). We could append hint into `result.attention.question` at the source? But we shouldn't mutate result.\n\nLet me think about what's most sensible: the takeover hint should be visible to the user, so a truncated 80-char line losing it is bad. For attention card the question is sent fully (SSE). For the report line, an 80-char cap is by design. Perhaps the hint goes at the fr