      "reasoning": "Now let me write the constants. Let me carefully draft text.\n\n### VERIFICATION_IRON_LAW (turn-gate.ts)\n\n```\n/**\n * 验证铁律（2026-11-10 批 12 §一.1，superpowers verification-before-completion 改写）。\n *\n * 为什么要有这一条：模型最容易犯的错不是做错，而是**没验就说好**——\"应该能过\"\"上次跑过\"\n * 一句话就把没跑的验证糊过去，人拿着假结论继续往下走比直接报错贵得多。运行时的闸门管不到\n * \"这句结论有没有证据\"，只能靠提示词把\"先跑、再看、后说\"钉成硬纪律。\n *\n * 固定字节：不含时间 / 会话 / 名字，只决定注不注。\n * 落点：总管 persona 段之后（lifecycle 的 section）与执事轮输入（partner-context）。\n */\nexport const VERIFICATION_IRON_LAW = [\n  \"【验证铁律】\",\n  \"- 这一轮里没有真的跑过验证，就不许说「完成了 / 修好了 / 通过了」。\",\n  \"- 五步门：先说清哪条命令能证明这句话 → 真跑 → 读完整个输出（看退出码、数失败数）→ 与结论对账 → 才下结论。\",\n  \"- 主张 ↔ 证据对照：\",\n  \"  · 说「测试通过」→ 要有 0 失败的输出；「上次跑过」「应该能过」不算。\",\n  \"  · 说「改好了」→ 要看到原症状已消失；只改了代码不算。\",\n  \"  · 说「做完了」→ 要有落盘的改动；自己说做完了不算。\",\n  \"  · 说「要求都满足了」→ 要逐条对着清单打勾；测试全绿不算。\",\n  \"- 红旗（出现即是在撒谎，回头去跑）：说「应该 / 大概 / 看起来没问题」；没跑就先说「很好 / 完成 / 搞定」；想「就这一次不用验」；累了想收工。\",\n].join(\"\\n\");\n```\nLength ≤500 chars? Count roughly: line1 6, line2 33, line3 55, line4 15, four 30-ish = 120, red flag 75. Total ~300. Fine.\n\n### RULING_DISCIPLINE\n\n```\nexport const RULING_DISCIPLINE = [\n  \"【裁决纪律】\",\n  \"- 继续干，别反复请示：「要不要我继续」是在浪费人的一天；计划里的事一口气做完。\",\n  \"- 只有四种情况停下问人：① 不可逆或破坏性的操作；② 安全敏感的动作；③ 工作目录之外的副作用（合并、推共享分支、发布）；④ 计划烂到往前每一步都是猜。\",\n  \"- 四停之外一律自己裁决，并记一行账：`裁决：<决定了什么> — <为什么> — <错了的代价>`；写进给主人的汇报或任务单留言，让人事后看得见、能推翻。\",\n  \"- 一个错的裁决，人看得见、也能让我改；一个卡着等回答的会话，花掉的是人一整天。\",\n].join(\"\\n\");\n```\n\n### TAKEOVER_HINT\n\n```\nexport const TAKEOVER_HINT = \"这类问题已经连着 3 次没解决，建议你来接手，或者换个说法重新派一次。\";\nexport function takeoverHintEnabled(): boolean { ... }\n```\n\n### REPORT_FOUR_LINES (delegation.ts)\n\n```\nexport const REPORT_FOUR_LINES = [\n  \"状态：完成 / 部分完成 / 卡住\",\n  \"结果：一句话说清做成了什么（不是过程）\",\n  \"证据：拿什么证明的（改了哪个文件 / 跑了什么命令 / 看到什么输出）\",\n  \"解锁：卡住时，下一步需要谁做什么；没卡住就写「无」\",\n].join(\"\\n\");\n```\nPlus a note about name and not sending back. Maybe a second constant `REPORT_FOUR_LINES_NOTE`? Task says \"外加两条：回报开头是队友的名字；不把任务发回给来源\". Could append to REPORT_FOUR_LINES after the block? But format should be exactly 4 lines. Better define guidance as a separate function/const? Use `REPORT_FOUR_LINES` exactly 4 lines, and in delegate description add: `\"派活前告诉工人按四行回报（开头写「给<你的名字>：」，且不要把任务原样发回给派活的人）：\\n\" + REPORT_FOUR_LINES`. That covers the two extra rules in prose.\n\n### WORK_SILENCE_DISCIPLINE\n\n```\nexport const WORK_SILENCE_DISCIPLINE = [\n  \"【干活期间】\",\n  \"- 接单确认只发一次，点名说清要干什么；之后干活期间不说话（不播报「我正在…」）。\",\n  \"- 再开口只有三种情况：有结果了 / 需要人做决定 / 干不完要交代。\",\n  \"- 交付物必须自己带着验收证据：改了哪个文件、跑了什么、看到什么。没有证据的「做完了」不算完成。\",\n].join(\"\\n\");\n```\n\n### ATTENTION_ONE_QUESTION\n\n```\nexport const ATTENTION_ONE_QUESTION = [\n  \"【提问纪律】\",\n  \"- 一次只问一个具体问题，别把三个问题塞进一段话。\",\n  \"- 问题要点名对象与期望：「第 2 条的标题你想要哪种：A / B」，不要问「这样可以吗」。\",\n  \"- 问题若是因为某条消息 / 某个文件引起的，点名那条消息或文件，别让人自己去回忆。\",\n].join(\"\\n\");\n```\n\nNow partner-context text assembly: currently returns contract, goal, status, guard. Add disciplines. Should they appear for chief too? partner-context is built for any partner session including chief. Fine.\n\nBut careful: buildPartnerStatusSection includes ATTENTION_REPLY_GUIDANCE. If no status, disciplines still inject (fixed bytes). Tests \"空态省略\" assert text === guard when no contract/status. That will break. Need to update that test: now text includes disciplines + guard. And the switch-off case asserts text === undefined — with disciplines always on, text never undefined. So update test to expect disciplines present with guard off.\n\nIs that acceptable? The test is asserting old behavior. We're changing deliberate behavior per task (inject into partner turn input regardless). Update test accordingly.\n\nOrder decision: contract → goal → disciplines → status → guard? Or contract → goal → status → disciplines → guard. The task says 执事轮输入; no order requirement. Cache-wise fixed prefix best: disciplines before status. But status already after goal and before guard. I'll do: contract, goal, disciplines(verification, ruling, workSilence, attentionOne), status, guard. Status includes ATTENTION_REPLY_GUIDANCE (dynamic presence). Hmm, then the fixed prefix ends before status. Good.\n\nWait, is it weird that verification iron law appears for partners and also chief (via lifecycle section)? Chief gets both? Chief partner turn context includes disciplines including verification; and lifecycle persona section also injects VERIFICATION_IRON_LAW for all conversations → chief gets it twice. Need to avoid duplication. Options: partner-context includes verification only for non-chief? Or lifecycle section only for non-partner sessions? \n\nTask: \"注入到总管 persona 段之后与执事轮输入两处\". 总管 = chief. If chief is also a partner session, double injection. Check whether chief sessions get partner context: lifecycle `partnerIdOfSession(conversationId)` returns chief's session id (linked). Yes probably. So I should skip verification in partner-context when partnerId === CHIEF_PARTNER_ID? But partner-context doesn't import chief constant currently; can import PARTNER_CONTRACT_SECTIONS already from partners, add CHIEF_PARTNER_ID.\n\nAlternatively make lifecycle section render only for chief/worker (non-partner) sessions? But requirement says after persona for chief. Simpler: in partner-context, include VERIFICATION_IRON_LAW only if partnerId !== CHIEF_PARTNER_ID. But for workers (worker persona, not partner) lifecycle section injects. For normal sessions too. Good, no duplicates.\n\nSimilarly RULING_DISCIPLINE only in partner-context + delegate description (tools, not prompt injection at runtime) — no dup.\n\nHmm, but chief in partner turn context also gets RULING/WORK_SILENCE/ATTENTION — intended.\n\nWait, do partner (non-chief) turns get persona section? No, persona section returns undefined for non-chief partner. So partner-context is their only injection. Good.\n\nNow lifecycle section key: add after persona:\n```ts\n{\n  key: \"verification_iron_law\",\n  render: () => VERIFICATION_IRON_LAW,\n},\n```\nAlways. For non-chief partner sessions this section also renders! Because section is global, persona renders undefined for partner but verification still renders → partner gets it from section AND partner-context (if we include for non-chief). Duplication again.\n\nNeed to decide: inject VERIFICATION via lifecycle for all sessions, and don't put it in partner-context? But task says \"与执事轮输入两处\". If lifecycle section already applies to partner conversations (same harness), then it's already in 执事轮输入. But \"执事轮输入\" specifically refers to buildPartnerTurnContext text. Hmm.\n\nBetter: lifecycle section renders only for non-partner sessions (partnerId null) OR chief? Chief needs after persona. And partner-context includes for non-chief partners. That satisfies both without duplication:\n- lifecycle section: if session belongs to non-chief partner → undefined; else (chief + normal + worker) inject.\n- partner-context: if partnerId !== chief → inject.\n\nThis adds a DB lookup in the section render, same pattern as persona section (uses partnerIdOfSession). Fine, it's every request though: one sqlite read — persona already does it. But section render result changes only on session type; durable caches by value.\n\nActually simpler alternative: section always injects for everyone, and partner-context doesn't include verification at all. Then partners also get it (via section) — satisfies \"执事轮输入\" functionally, but test asserting partner-context text includes it would fail. Task's explicit \"两处\" suggests two assembly points. I'll do the conditional approach.\n\nHmm, but the conditional check for \"non-chief partner\" in lifecycle duplicates logic. Reuse pattern:\n\n```ts\n{\n  key: \"verification_iron_law\",\n  render: (input) => {\n    if (COMPANIONS_ENABLED) {\n      try {\n        const partnerId = partnersStore().partnerIdOfSession(Number(input.conversationId));\n        if (partnerId && partnerId !== CHIEF_PARTNER_ID) return undefined;\n      } catch {}\n    }\n    return VERIFICATION_IRON_LAW;\n  },\n},\n```\nComment: 执事轮（非总管）由 partner-context 注入，这里跳过避免重复.\n\nNow RULING_DISCIPLINE in partner-context: chief and partners both — no duplicate since not in lifecycle.\n\nNow the four-line report: where does 总管/执事 see it? Only delegate description. Also maybe append to partner-context? Requirement 3 says \"改 delegation.ts 里给执事/总管看的汇报口径（formatReport 相关文案旁加常量 REPORT_FOUR_LINES）\". The constant placement only; consumption is tool desc. But \"给执事/总管看的汇报口径\" implies the planner must tell workers. Description covers it. Could also inject REPORT_FOUR_LINES into partner-context? Not asked. Keep to description.\n\nHmm — but delegate tool is available to chief and partners; description is prompt. Fine.\n\nNow failure-streak module. Let me write it.\n\n```ts\n/**\n * 同类失败连击（2026-11-10 批 12 §一.4，对应七 #6 = 三#5）。\n *\n * 为什么要有：运行时已经有防打转（同一次工具调用重复）与重派次数（countRetries），\n * 但没有\"同一个来源在同一个类别上连续栽三次\"的记账——模型会一直换着花样试，\n * 人却不知道这活已经卡了很久。到第三次就该把决定权交回人手里。\n *\n * 纯状态、可序列化：不碰文件、不碰时间，落盘与清理交给调用方；进程内单例只做\n * 一次低成本的连击计数（重启即清零，符合\"连续\"的语义）。\n */\nexport const FAILURE_STREAK_THRESHOLD = 3;\nexport const FAILURE_CATEGORIES = [\"tool-error\", \"timeout\", \"rejected\", \"needs_you\", \"unresolved\"] as const;\nexport type FailureCategory = (typeof FAILURE_CATEGORIES)[number];\n\nexport interface FailureStreakSnapshot {\n  counts: Record<string, number>;\n  hinted: string[];\n}\n\nconst SEP = \"\\u0000\";\nfunction keyOf(source, category) { return `${source}${SEP}${category}`; }\n\nexport class FailureStreak {\n  private counts = new Map<string, number>();\n  private hinted = new Set<string>();\n\n  recordFailure(source, category): { count: number; suggestTakeover: boolean } {\n    const key = keyOf(source, category);\n    const count = (this.counts.get(key) ?? 0) + 1;\n    this.counts.set(key, count);\n    if (count >= FAILURE_STREAK_THRESHOLD && !this.hinted.has(key)) {\n      this.hinted.add(key);\n      return { count, suggestTakeover: true };\n    }\n    return { count, suggestTakeover: false };\n  }\n\n  /** 成功一次即清零：同一来源的所有类别一起清（这个来源已经不卡了）。 */\n  recordSuccess(source): void {\n    const prefix = `${source}${SEP}`;\n    for (const key of [...this.counts.keys()]) if (key.startsWith(prefix)) this.counts.delete(key);\n    for (const key of [...this.hinted]) if (key.startsWith(prefix)) this.hinted.delete(key);\n  }\n\n  countOf(source, category): number { return this.counts.get(keyOf(source, category)) ?? 0; }\n\n  serialize(): FailureStreakSnapshot { ... }\n  static restore(snapshot): FailureStreak\n}\n\nconst shared = new FailureStreak();\nexport function failureStreak(): FailureStreak { return shared; }\nexport function resetFailureStreak(): void { ... }  // tests?\nexport function takeoverHintEnabled(): boolean\n```\n\nShould hint re-arm? Once hinted, stays until success. Test \"3 次触发 / 中间成功一次则不触发\". Test: fail,fail,success,fail,fail,fail → third after reset triggers. Good.\n\nNote: `countOf` isn't strictly needed but useful for tests? Tests can use recordFailure return. Keep minimal: recordFailure, recordSuccess, serialize/restore (requirement says serializable). Add countOf maybe not. \"纯状态（可序列化）\" — provide snapshot. Keep `toJSON`? I'll include serialize/restore and countOf for tests/UI; minimal.\n\nSerialization restore: parse keys with `key.lastIndexOf(SEP)`. Source could theoretically contain SEP (unlikely); use lastIndexOf to preserve full source. Store counts record keyed by encoded string; serialize just `Object.fromEntries(this.counts)`.\n\nNow wire into delegation.ts:\n- import { failureStreak, takeoverHintEnabled } from \"./failure-streak.ts\";\n- import TAKEOVER_HINT from \"./agent/turn-gate.ts\"? delegation.ts importing agent/turn-gate might create cycle: turn-gate imports approvals only. delegation doesn't import agent currently (it's imported by agent). `agent/turn-gate.ts` imports ../approvals; approvals might import delegation? Let me check. If turn-gate imports approvals, approvals imports...?",
