        "text": "Fine.\n\nNow buildPartnerTurnContext signature: add disciplines. Need imports in partner-context from delegation (WORK_SILENCE_DISCIPLINE, ATTENTION_ONE_QUESTION, RULING_DISCIPLINE?) — RULING_DISCIPLINE lives in turn-gate. partner-context imports from \"./turn-gate.ts\" and \"../delegation.ts\".\n\nWait: turn-gate.ts is in agent/; partner-context also agent/. Fine.\n\nAdd fields to PartnerTurnContext? Add `discipline: string` maybe. Simpler compute inline and include in text; but tests may want. Add `discipline: string` field? Task doesn't require. Keep interface minimal: add optional? I'll add `discipline: string` so test can assert injection separately. Hmm, adding field is fine and useful. But \"不做无关\". I'll add since it clarifies assembly. Actually keep it simple: no new field; test asserts text includes constants. The interface doc says text only 后三段; update comment.\n\nOrder in text: contract, goal, discipline, status, guard. For non-chief partner include verification in discipline; for chief not.\n\nWait: chief gets VERIFICATION from lifecycle section. But does chief session get `buildPartnerTurnContext`? Yes if partnerIdOfSession returns chief. Let me verify partnerIdOfSession behavior for chief."
