        "text": "Use store.ensureChief(\"你是总管。\") then linkSession chief->606. Then buildPartnerTurnContext(\"chief\", 606) and assert discipline lacks 验证铁律 but has others. Also lifecycle section not directly unit-tested (hard). We can test the constant existence and that partner-context includes for non-chief. Assertion \"注入\" for lifecycle would need harness; but partner-context covers. For the lifecycle section, can we export a helper? It's inline in sections array. Could extract `verificationSectionFor(conversationId)` function in lifecycle and test? That's more code. The task says each new injection needs an assertion test. For VERIFICATION at lifecycle, the partner-context test asserts it for partners, but chief path goes through lifecycle section. We could add a test in partner-context that chief excludes, plus a test that constant is present in the section? Maybe export a small function `verificationIronLawFor(conversationId)` from lifecycle and use it in the section; then test. But importing lifecycle in a test boots a lot (harness?). Let's check lifecycle exports; module-level maybe heavy. Tests already avoid importing lifecycle except via agent. Hmm.\n\nAlternative: extract section render into a tiny exported pure helper in turn-gate? e.g. `verificationIronLawFor(partnerId: string | null)`. Then lifecycle uses it with resolved partnerId. Unit test asserts partner → undefined, chief/null → text. That's clean and testable without loading lifecycle. Do this in turn-gate.ts:\n\n```ts\nexport function verificationIronLawFor(partnerId: string | null): string | undefined {\n  return partnerId && partnerId !== \"chief\" ? undefined : VERIFICATION_IRON_LAW;\n}\n```\nBut importing CHIEF_PARTNER_ID from partners into turn-gate may create cycle? partners imports memory only. turn-gate → partners fine? partners doesn't import agent. But agent.ts imports both. OK. Yet turn-gate is meant to be pure; import constant is fine.\n\nHmm, but partner-context also needs the same logic. Reuse this helper in partner-context: `verificationIronLawFor(partnerId)`. And lifecycle: resolve partnerId then call. That centralizes.\n\nBut the lifecycle section also needs the partner lookup. Keep lookup there, call helper. Test helper in prompt-discipline.test.ts. Good.\n\nAdd helper to turn-gate with import CHIEF_PARTNER_ID from \"../partners.ts\". Check cycle: partners.ts → memory; no turn-gate. Fine.\n\nHowever, importing partners.ts into turn-gate pulls sqlite module on any turn-gate import (already loaded in server anyway). Test imports turn-gate → partners → node:sqlite, fine.\n\nAlternatively avoid import by comparing literal? No, use constant.\n\nLet me add."
      }
