      {
        "type": "reasoning_text",
        "text": "Now add tests. First failure-streak.test.ts:\n1. 3 times triggers once (3rd true, 4th false)\n2. success resets (fail fail success fail fail fail → third group triggers)\n3. different categories independent\n4. switch bypass (takeoverHintEnabled false for false/0/off)\n5. serialize/restore.\n\nThen prompt-discipline.test.ts:\n- constants fixed bytes (no date/time/session names), content assertions, lengths\n- partner context injection: disciplines all present, order (discipline before status), chief excludes verification\n- delegate description includes REPORT_FOUR_LINES + RULING_DISCIPLINE\n- formatReport takeover appends hint; without option unchanged\n- startDelegation wiring: 3 needs_you triggers attention question + report line, switch bypass, success resets.\n\nMaybe split delegation wiring into delegation.test.ts? New file prompt-discipline.test.ts is fine and must be added to test script.\n\nFor startDelegation test, need runtime with run emitting ticket then resolving. Let me model from delegation.test.ts.\n\nWe must be careful with the module singleton: use unique domain \"streak-e2e\" to avoid interfering. Also recordSuccess side effects on that domain only.\n\nTest sequence:\n```ts\nasync function runNeedsYou(domain, conversationId) {\n  const events=[];\n  const reports=[];\n  const { outcome } = startDelegation({conversationId, domain, requirement:\"x\"}, {\n    run: (_req, options) => {\n      options.onEvent?.({type:\"ticket\", ticketId:`T-${n}`, message:\"已受理\"});\n      return Promise.resolve({ticketId:`T-${n}`, status:\"needs_you\", line:\"等你\", attention:{kind:\"need_decision\", question:\"选哪个？\"}});\n    },\n    emit: (_c,e)=>events.push(e),\n    report: (_c,r)=>reports.push(r),\n    autoReport: true,\n  });\n  await outcome;\n  return {events, reports};\n}\n```\nNote: settle is called via accepted.promise.then(settle) — await outcome resolves on promise but settle attached via then; ordering: `.then(settle)` registered before caller awaits? `startDelegation` attaches `accepted.promise.then(settle).catch(...)`; caller awaits `outcome` which is accepted.promise — both callbacks run in registration order; settle registered first, so by the time await resolves, settle has run. In existing tests they await and assert events; fine.\n\nFor 1st/2nd: attention question exactly. 3rd: contains TAKEOVER_HINT and report.text contains \"建议你来接手\" maybe truncated. Use short question \"选哪个？\" to keep under 80. head 【任务 T-3 · streak-e2e】 = about 17 chars. body 9 + 5 + （hint 35） ≈ 66 + 17 = 83 > 80. Hmm. truncate would cut ending \"重新派一次。\" but \"建议你来接手\" survives. Assert report.text includes \"建议你来接手\". Good.\n\nSwitch bypass: set AGENT_TAKEOVER_HINT=\"false\" before 3 failures; question has no hint. But then hinted flag already set from previous test if same streak key. Use different domain for switch test, or reset. Export a reset? I can use fresh domains per subtest.\n\nSuccess reset: domain unique: fail fail done fail fail → no hint; third fail after that → hint.\n\nWait \"中间成功一次则不触发\": fail fail done fail fail → count 2. Then another fail → count 3 → hint. Test that sequence.\n\nImplementation detail: `takeoverHintEnabled()` is read at settle time, so env toggling works.\n\nNow writing test files. Need TicketResult attention type. Use `attention: { kind: \"need_decision\", question: \"...\" }`.\n\nReport type has text.\n\nLet me check TicketResult shape quickly."
      }
    ],
