      "reasoning": "Wait restore test: dirty counts key \"bad\" (no SEP) → splitKey returns source \"bad\", category \"\" → category invalid → dropped. Good.\n\nNow prompt-discipline.test.ts. Need createTools deps and a temp partner store for context injection? Simpler reuse PartnerContext test style with temp store. But making a partner requires sqlite temp dir. Fine.\n\nTests:\n1. constants content/length/fixed bytes:\n   - VERIFICATION_IRON_LAW includes key phrases, ≤500 chars, no date/time.\n   - RULING_DISCIPLINE includes 四停 and 裁决.\n   - WORK_SILENCE_DISCIPLINE.\n   - ATTENTION_ONE_QUESTION.\n   - REPORT_FOUR_LINES has 4 lines and exact prefixes.\n   - TAKEOVER_HINT.\n   All no dynamic date/time regex.\n\n2. Injected into partner turn input: build store, link session, context.text includes each (verification, ruling, work silence, attention), and order contract/... maybe status absent. Assert index(discipline) < index(【材料安全】) and status order if ticket exists. Simpler assert text includes all four headers.\n\n3. chief exclusion: store.ensureChief, linkSession chief id 606, context.discipline excludes 验证铁律 but includes others; verificationIronLawFor(\"chief\") === VERIFICATION, verificationIronLawFor(\"uuid\") === undefined, verificationIronLawFor(null) === text.\n\n4. delegate description: createTools(makeDeps({delegate:true})) find tool. Description includes REPORT_FOUR_LINES and RULING_DISCIPLINE and \"给<你的名字>\". Need MemoryScope mock.\n\n5. formatReport takeover: needs_you short question. Without options text equals old. With takeover contains 建议你来接手.\n\n6. startDelegation wiring: 3 needs_you same domain → third attention question contains hint and report text contains 建议你来接手; first two not. Then switch off with new domain → no hint. Then success reset.\n\nThis file imports delegation.ts which imports turn-gate and failure-streak. Fine.\n\nCareful: importing tools.ts pulls chancellor and maybe env. createTools with delegate might need receipts DB? Let's check delegate tool construction — does it read env at module/creation time? Existing tool-capability test calls createTools(delegate:true) fine.\n\nThe delegate tool description is built at createTools time; domainList() reads chancellorWorkRoot (could touch FS? listManagers might read dir; harmless). Existing tests do it.\n\nNow write. For temp store, use same pattern.\n\nFor startDelegation tests, runtime.run returns resolved promise; but `translate` needs to set ticketId synchronously. We'll emit ticket event synchronously in run before return. Use unique ticket ids.\n\nLet me write the test file.",
