      "messageId": "01a1c0a7461d78b297555b661143fa00",
      "stepSeq": 77,
      "reasoning": "Logic is right for uuid → undefined. Wait no: partnerId=\"uuid\" truthy && !=chief → true → undefined. That means ordinary partners get undefined, chief gets text. I intended the opposite! Lifecycle injects for chief; partner-context injects for non-chief. So helper should be used differently at each site, or the helper semantics should be \"should lifecycle inject\". I defined it as \"who gets it in lifecycle\" (chief/null). And partner-context needs the inverse. Better rename/param: `verificationIronLawFor(partnerId)` should mean \"is this session covered here\", used in both? Can't be both.\n\nCleaner: helper takes `partnerId` and returns iron law for **non-chief** partners? Then lifecycle must invert. Hmm.\n\nBest: `verificationIronLawFor(partnerId: string | null, owner: \"lifecycle\" | \"partner\")`? Overkill.\n\nDefine helper as the single source of who the verification belongs to: \n```\nexport function verificationIronLawFor(partnerId): string | undefined // 执事轮输入用：非总管执事有，总管/无身份没有\n```\nThen lifecycle uses `partnerId && partnerId !== chief ? undefined : VERIFICATION`. That's inverted inline, but then helper test semantics clear.\n\nSimpler: rename to `partnerVerificationIronLaw(partnerId)` returning text only for non-chief. Lifecycle calls `verificationOwnedByPersona(partnerId)`. Two tiny functions? \n\nLet me do:\n```\nexport function verificationIronLawFor(partnerId: string | null): string | undefined {\n  // 执事轮（partner-context）用：只有非总管执事在这里补\n  return partnerId && partnerId !== CHIEF_PARTNER_ID ? VERIFICATION_IRON_LAW : undefined;\n}\nexport function lifecycleOwnsVerification(partnerId: string | null): boolean {\n  return !partnerId || partnerId === CHIEF_PARTNER_ID;\n}\n```\nLifecycle uses `lifecycleOwnsVerification(partnerId) ? VERIFICATION_IRON_LAW : undefined`.\n\nUpdate test accordingly:\n- verificationIronLawFor(null) === undefined\n- (\"chief\") === undefined\n- (\"partner-uuid\") === VERIFICATION\n- lifecycleOwnsVerification checks.\n\nLet me fix.",
      "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash",
      "requestModelId": "deepseek-v4.1-flash",
      "requestModelName": "DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash",
      "traceId": "00033f358c6984484a581f8c0bd9c39b",
