      "reasoning": "Potential issue: `formatReport` appends hint inside 80-char truncation. In my e2e test with question \"选哪个？\" the hint survived \"建议你来接手\" but likely the tail was cut. Acceptable but the task said append a sentence. Better to ensure the full sentence appears. Options:\n- For takeover, allow 160 chars. But 80 is a documented cap. Could instead put TAKEOVER_HINT at the front of body for needs_you: `建议你接手：这类问题...` then truncate; tail still cut.\n- Reduce head? no.\n\nWhat matters is the user sees the suggestion. \"建议你来接手\" is within. But \"或者换个说法重新派一次\" might be cut. Let me compute exact length for test: 【任务 T-s3 · batch12-streak-hint】 = 2+2+1+4+3+18+1 ≈ 29 chars. body: \"有一项需要你处理：\" 9 + \"选哪个？\" 4 + \"（\" 1 + hint 36? + \"）\" 1 = ~51 → total 80. Actually maybe just fits! Let me check actual report text in test? Not printed. Could assert full TAKEOVER_HINT inclusion. Let me compute hint length: \"这类问题已经连着 3 次没解决，建议你来接手，或者换个说法重新派一次。\" \ncount: 这类(2)问题(2)=4 已经(2)=6 连着(2)=8 空格(1)=9 3=10 空格=11 次没解决(4)=15 ，=16 建议你来接手(6)=22 ，=23 或者换个说法重新派一次(12)=35 。=36. So 36. Head for T-s3+batch12-streak-hint: 【=1 任务=2 空格=1 T-s3=4 空格=1 ·=1 空格=1 batch12-streak-hint=19 】=1 → 31. Body 9+4+2+36=51. Total 82 > 80 by 2 → cut \"次。\" maybe. \"重新派一\" survives mostly. Assert full hint would fail.\n\nFor real domains usually shorter (e.g. \"frontend\"), then total = 1+2+1+4+1+1+1+8+1 = 20 + 51 = 71 → full. Test domain long causes truncation. Fine; test asserts \"建议你来接手\".\n\nCould improve by making report text append hint after truncating base to fit: `truncate(head+body_without_hint, 80 - hint.length - 2) + （hint）` guaranteeing hint fully visible. That's better UX and meets \"append sentence\". Let me implement: for needs_you with takeover, build base then reserve space:\n\n```ts\nconst hint = options.takeover ? `（${TAKEOVER_HINT}）` : \"\";\nconst body = ...\ntext: truncate(`${head}${body}${hint}`, options.takeover ? 140 : 80) ?\n```\nChanging cap is uglier. Alternative: when takeover, truncate question itself:\n```\nconst full = `${head}${body}${hint}`;\nif (options.takeover) {\n  const kept = truncate(`${head}${body}`, Math.max(1, 80 - hint.length));\n  text = `${kept}${hint}`; // could still exceed 80 if head+... \n}\n```\n80-38=42 chars for head+body, which would cut domain/question heavily but keeps hint. Hmm. 42 chars: head ~20, leaves 22 for body. It'd cut the question a lot.\n\nMaybe the right call is: the takeover hint replaces the standard prefix. Body = `建议你接手：${question}` + hint? Duplicate.\n\nHonestly, the 80-char cap conflicts. I'll keep as is and note the boundary in changelog (already noted). The user sees \"建议你来接手\" which is the actionable part. Good enough.\n\nNext concern: `TAKEOVER_HINT` imported into delegation.ts from agent/turn-gate.ts. Does this create an import cycle through agent/turn-gate → partners → ...? partners.ts doesn't import delegation. approvals doesn't. OK.\n\nBut arch direction: delegation.ts (root) → agent/ is a bit odd but no rule. Alternatively move TAKEOVER_HINT into failure-streak.ts to avoid, but task explicitly says turn-gate. Keep.\n\nNow: partner-context imports turn-gate which imports partners (for CHIEF_PARTNER_ID) — partner-context already imports partners; fine.\n\nOne more: `buildPartnerDisciplineSection` is called for chief and includes RULING etc. The docstring says \"总管（chief）的验证铁律由 lifecycle 注入\". Good.\n\nCheck the new context test at line ~289 expects `context.text === `${discipline}\\n\\n${guard}``. But contract is null after bumpContract with headings only; goal null; status null. text = discipline + guard. Passed earlier? We ran full tests before this change? We changed nothing after full test except console.log removal. Full test passed with this assertion. Good.\n\nNow check tools.ts description diff. And test file issue: `DelegationEvent` filter with type narrowing works. Full test passed.\n\nPotential concern: in delegation `settle`, for `needs_you` result where `result.attention` is undefined, `takeover` true appends hint only in report (question || line). Fine.\n\nAnother concern: repeated `needs_you` on the same ticket (续跑) counts as consecutive failures. That's intended (\"同类问题连着3次没解决\").\n\nNow check whether `AGENT_TAKEOVER_HINT` should be added to the flags whitelist / interface doc env table. The task says switch `AGENT_TAKEOVER_HINT` default true. AGENTS says env table lives in 接口文档 §6. Do we need to add env docs? Batch tasks usually do. Let's check 接口文档 §6 env table and whether recent switches are listed. The task doesn't explicitly require, but \"契约与文档一致\" and env table is a baseline doc. Since new env var, should add a row. Let me inspect §6.",
